{"availability":"available","full":"oreilles/polars-st","name":"polars-st","description":"Geospatial extension for Polars DataFrames.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":202,"forks":12,"created":"2024-09-20T09:07:04Z","updated":"2026-10-08T10:08:00Z","license":"LGPL-2.1","branch":"main","homepage":"https://oreilles.github.io/polars-st/","topics":["dataframe","geodataframe","geospatial","gis","polars","python","rust"],"demo":"https://oreilles.github.io/polars-st/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.323Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.323Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.323Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.323Z","stars":202,"forks":12}],"technologies":["Python","Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Polars ST provides spatial operations on Polars DataFrames, Series, and Expressions. Just like Shapely and GeoPandas, it make use of the GEOS library, meaning that its API is mostly identical to theirs.","GeoPolars is an very promising tool for manipulating geographic data in Polars based on the GeoArrow specification. It however seems to be quite a long way from being ready and feature-complete, mostly due to Polars lack of support for Arrow Extension Types and subclassing of core datatypes.","polars-st stores geometry as EWKB in regular Binary columns and delegates core functionality to GEOS, which allows it to be ready now, with full support for Z / M coordinates, curved geometry types (CircularString, CurvePolygon, ...) and Series with mixed geometry type and SRIDs."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/oreilles/polars-st/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"72836a15791d6bcdfecedc5de39f0b0f368ec3a060cce7ec1934308d8bcc5e32","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.465Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.465Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Polars ST provides spatial operations on Polars DataFrames, Series, and Expressions. Just like Shapely and